<title>PHILIPPINES: Asiatrust makes debut at 43.50 pesos.</title>
<headline>Asiatrust makes debut at 43.50 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asiatrust Bank jumped by nine percent to 43.50 pesos on its debut on Tuesday on the Philippine Stock Exchange from its offering price of 39.88 pesos, brokers said.  </p>
<p>&quot;I'm happy with the opening salvo of Asiatrust,&quot; said Kevin Khoe at Sapphire Securities.</p>
<p>Khoe predicted earlier that the issue could reach a high of 43 pesos on its debut.</p>
<p>&quot;Prospects for Asiatrust are bright because its a niche player in consumer-banking,&quot; Khoe said, adding that the bank's target clients are wealthy Filipino-Chinese businessmen.</p>
<p>About 554,000 shares of the bank changed hands at the open.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
